From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=81ngel=20Ren=C3=A9?=
 <17342133+angelrenefm@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:57:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: s5p-mfc: let dynamic DPB clients queue more capture
 buffers
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The CAPTURE queue is capped at the minimum the stream needs plus
MFC_MAX_EXTRA_DPB (5). That fits a fixed DPB, which the firmware takes
whole at INIT_BUFFERS. With dynamic DPB (MFC v15) the firmware only
holds the frames it still references or has not shown yet, and every
other buffer the client keeps, a player's display queue among them,
comes out of those five.

mpv 0.41 on the Pixel 7 shows the problem: with its default gpu-next
output it keeps more decoded frames queued than the five spare ones,
the decoder runs out of free buffers after the first frame and the
picture freezes. With dynamic DPB, cap the queue at MFC_MAX_BUFFERS
(32) only, the driver's own limit for any queue; FFmpeg's
h264_v4l2m2m asks for 20 by default. vb2 already falls back to fewer
buffers when the memory runs short.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ángel René <17342133+angelrenefm@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c
index 6d7f093b4..653f7efa6 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c
@@ -966,7 +966,8 @@ static int s5p_mfc_queue_setup(struct vb2_queue *vq,
 		/* Setup buffer count */
 		if (*buf_count < ctx->pb_count)
 			*buf_count = ctx->pb_count;
-		if (*buf_count > ctx->pb_count + MFC_MAX_EXTRA_DPB)
+		if (!dev->dynamic_dpb &&
+		    *buf_count > ctx->pb_count + MFC_MAX_EXTRA_DPB)
 			*buf_count = ctx->pb_count + MFC_MAX_EXTRA_DPB;
 		if (*buf_count > MFC_MAX_BUFFERS)
 			*buf_count = MFC_MAX_BUFFERS;
